# Blacklist for the R6 check (agnosticism principle).
#
# This .example file is a template. Copy it to `tools/agnostic-blacklist.txt`
# and add your own project-specific names. The `agnostic-blacklist.txt` itself is
# under .gitignore — each fork keeps its own.
#
# Format: one pattern per line. Case-insensitive substring match.
# Lines starting with # are comments. Empty lines are ignored.
#
# Purpose: keep project-specific terms from leaking into export/CLAUDE.md
# and its import graph. The hook fires at the warning level — it is a safety net,
# not a block. The final decision stays with the human.
#
# What to put HERE:
#   - names of specific projects
#   - names of clients, business domains, private terms
#   - explicit stack bindings, if such a stack must not appear globally
#
# What NOT to put here:
#   - generic words that may occur in a neutral context
#     (for example "TypeScript" — may be mentioned, but not as a mandatory stack)


# === Project names ===
# (add your own here)
